@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] build-v2-opt-in
The crate MUST remain independent of production v1 until a separately validated caller cutover.
A0 schemas MUST NOT decide cache hits, launch native tools or publish results.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-identity-boundary
Identity ingredients MUST distinguish producing input keys from each output's content digest.
Provenance MUST remain outside identity ingredients. Installed Python, dependencies, lockfiles,
Blender/add-ons, Unreal and compiler/SDK versions MUST NOT automatically become key ingredients;
platform invalidation uses explicit cache/op versions. See tests/interfaces.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-wire-boundary
Worker messages MUST use a separate pipe with a versioned, bounded JSON frame. Unknown message
shapes, unsupported protocol versions and truncated frames MUST fail, as MUST duplicate keys and
positional (array) forms of the envelope, message or any typed record; arrays inside params and
lists remain data. Only EOF between frames may be a clean close. Bulk asset bytes MUST travel in
staged files, not wire messages. See tests/protocol.rs and the shared vectors
tests/vectors/protocol_v1.json checked by tests/worker_session.rs and
platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_protocol.py.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-t0-registry
CI MUST compile the current crate successfully before running its T0 tests. Its matrix MUST cover
all declared supported host platforms. Every active scenario MUST have complete, unskipped execution
evidence on each applicable platform within ten seconds, excluding compilation. Other-platform
exclusions and pending future scenarios MUST be reported separately and MUST NOT count as coverage.
See tools/check_registry.py and platform/studio/tests/test_build_v2_registry.py.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-object-digest-format
Object format version 1 MUST name payload bytes with exactly 64 lowercase SHA-256 hex characters
under objects/sha256. A change to algorithm or encoding MUST use a new object format/namespace.
Filesystem permissions MUST remain result metadata rather than payload identity.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-object-publication
The object store MUST freeze and verify an independent clone before atomic no-replace publication.
Caller-provided unchecked digests MUST NOT certify bytes. Hits MUST clone without rehashing or
scanning output folders; clone failures MUST be explicit and MUST NOT fall back to byte copies.
Existing entries and unrelated checkout/staging files MUST never be overwritten or removed.
See tests/objects.rs; macOS APFS tests are required acceptance evidence.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-worker-session-order
A controller session MUST accept work only after a hello with the expected worker version, MUST
keep at most one active job, and MUST require `started` then exactly one terminal response with
the active job ID. Wrong IDs, duplicate or out-of-order responses, malformed frames and early end
of stream MUST break the session. Sending `cancel` MUST NOT count as cancellation; only a worker's
`cancelled` failure confirms it. A worker MUST send `started` for every `run` before its single
terminal response, including a job it rejects at once and a `cancel` that arrives before it started.
Job requests MUST pass through unchanged. See tests/worker_session.rs.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-result-leases
Result writes MUST have a durable staging lease before payload creation and durable object claims
under the shared metadata mutex before object publication. The order MUST be objects, immutable
result record, required durable build-root callback, then per-unit claim release. Failure before
durable rooting MUST retain claims; no failure may erase earlier results. Live or unknown owners/workers MUST prevent reclamation;
timestamps alone MUST NOT expire leases. See tests/results.rs; B4/B5 implement root/GC policy later.
Initial leases MUST retain supplied upstream result keys while the consumer record is incomplete.
Fresh lease/staging names MUST preserve every occupied entry, including dangling symlinks.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] build-v2-frozen-result-validation
Output validators MUST read the same frozen snapshots hashed and published by B1. Result winner
comparison MUST include complete fixed and group manifests/projections and semantic modes, but
exclude provenance, unit scheduling labels and upstream retention links. Group publication MUST
require complete actual membership, fixed keyed contracts and sealed frozen-source validation.
External outputs MUST refuse until their typed adapter exists. Cached group tokens MUST issue
only after named object checks and durable pins under the GC mutex, without plan reads, output
tree walks or rehashing. See tests/results.rs and
groups::tests::leased_group_publication_restores_tokens_and_compares_whole_manifest.
